Package: mouse-finder
Version: 1.1.0
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Alexander Rozhkov <2246636@gmail.com>
Depends: libgtk-3-0, libxcursor1, libx11-6, libcairo2, libglib2.0-0, libayatana-appindicator3-1, udev
Homepage: https://github.com/LoginByCall/mouse-finder
Description: Shake to find mouse for Ubuntu (X11 and Wayland)
 macOS-style shake-to-find-mouse tray application for Ubuntu. Shake the
 mouse quickly left and right — the cursor temporarily enlarges so you can
 spot it on the screen. Includes settings dialog and autostart. Reads mouse
 motion directly from /dev/input, so it works under both X11 and Wayland
 sessions. Written in C; no Python or runtime dependencies beyond system
 GTK3 libs.
